## Regression Concepts Explained

### 1. Correlation Coefficient (r)

| r value | Interpretation | Example |
|---------|----------------|---------|
| +0.9 to +1.0 | Strong positive | Study hours → Exam score |
| +0.5 to +0.9 | Moderate positive | | 
| 0 to +0.5 | Weak positive | |
| 0 | No linear relationship | Random data |
| -0.5 to 0 | Weak negative | |
| -0.9 to -0.5 | Moderate negative | |
| -1.0 to -0.9 | Strong negative | Temperature → Heating bill |

### 2. Linear Regression Equation

```
y = mx + b

Where:
- y = predicted value (Dependent variable) → Exam Score
- x = input value (Independent variable) → Study Hours
- m = slope (Coefficient) → How much y changes per unit x
- b = intercept → Value of y when x = 0
```

### 3. R² Score (Coefficient of Determination)

| R² Value | Meaning |
|----------|---------|
| 1.0 | Perfect fit (model explains 100% of variance) |
| 0.8-0.99 | Strong fit |
| 0.5-0.8 | Moderate fit |
| 0-0.5 | Weak fit |
| 0 | Model explains nothing |

