## Key Takeaways
1. **Visual inspection first** - Always plot your data before modeling
2. **Correlation ≠ Causation** - Even strong correlation doesn't prove causation
3. **Outliers matter** - A single outlier can completely change regression results
4. **R² isn't everything** - Always check residuals and model assumptions
5. **Noise reduces model fit** - Real-world data always has some noise
